course: dictionary
lesson: 5800
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. «Madeira» is a good example. It can be a place, a drink, or a cake.
explain: «The ukulele grew out of small Portuguese guitars brought to Hawaii by immigrants from Madeira in the 1870s and 1880s.» The words immigrants and brought show that Madeira is a place people came from, so it means the islands. Always check by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: A capital M usually means a place, as in the islands. Madeira cake is a different thing: a plain, firm sponge cake that people in Britain eat with a cup of tea. Its name comes from the wine, but the cake has no wine in it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Madeira» is a group of islands in the Atlantic Ocean that belong to Portugal.
fact: The Madeira islands are famous for mountains, flowers and a warm climate.
fact: «Madeira» can also mean a strong, sweet wine made on those islands.
fact: «Madeira cake» is a plain, firm sponge cake, often eaten with a cup of tea in the UK.
exercise: The ukulele grew out of small Portuguese guitars brought to Hawaii by immigrants from «Madeira». What is Madeira here? | A strong, sweet wine | A type of guitar | *A group of islands in the Atlantic Ocean | A plain sponge cake
exercise: At the party, Mum cuts a slice of «Madeira cake» and hands it round with tea. What kind of thing is it? | A group of islands | A flower from the mountains | *A plain, firm sponge cake | A strong, sweet wine
exercise: Ella says, «Madeira is warm and full of flowers.» What does Madeira mean? | *A place, a group of islands | A bird that sings at night | A kind of tea | A firm cake with no taste
test: «Pour a small glass of Madeira after dinner.» What does Madeira mean here? | A type of guitar | A plain sponge cake | A group of islands in the Atlantic | *A strong, sweet wine
test: Does «Madeira cake» have wine in it? | Yes, the islands make it | *No, it is a plain sponge cake, named after the wine | Yes, it is soaked in strong wine | Yes, it is decorated with flowers
exam: Which clues in «Madeira is famous for mountains and flowers» show that Madeira is a place? | Plain and firm | Strong and sweet | *Mountains and flowers | Eaten with a cup of tea
